H-atoms (H of strongly-connected primes) per size:
  size 1: SC primes have H in [1]
  size 2: SC primes have H in []
  size 3: SC primes have H in [3]
  size 4: SC primes have H in [5]
  size 5: SC primes have H in [9, 11, 13, 15]
  size 6: SC primes have H in [15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45]

verify H multiplicative over condensation (n=5,6):
  n=5: H == product over primes for ALL 12 classes: True
  n=6: H == product over primes for ALL 56 classes: True

=> H(tournament) = PRODUCT of H over its strongly-connected primes (the recursive
   compression: factor into SC atoms, look up each atom's H). The atoms are the
   incompressible cores; everything reducible multiplies cleanly.
